{"name":"Shanghai","slug":"shanghai","region":"East Asia","lat":31.23,"lon":121.47,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Shanghai has warmed by about 0.25 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.9 °C in all, with the coldest days warming fastest, so cold extremes are becoming rarer. El Niño has no identifiable effect on Dec–Feb temperature. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a wetter season with more rainy days, and this year's shift is substantial. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.4 points per decade, roughly 3 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 70% chance), about 0.8 °C above the 1991–2020 average, mostly because of the long-term warming trend rather than El Niño; a wetter-than-normal season is likely (about 70% chance), and a more humid season than normal is more likely than not (about 55%). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":6.4682,"trend_per_decade":0.2501,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.8759,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1533,"enso_p":0.1843,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0243,"intrinsic_sd":0.9095,"effect_this_season":0.3878,"effect_ratio":0.4264,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.7834,"forecast_mean":7.2516,"forecast_sd":0.9858,"p_below":0.1035,"p_near":0.1856,"p_above":0.7109,"forecast_words":"Likely (71%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"trend_part_2027":0.3956,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":15.5049,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.3427,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0966,"enso_p":0.5259,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.2445,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.2415,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1318,"enso_p":0.2972,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.3336,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.1847,"trend_p":0.001,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.275,"enso_p":0.0859,"confidence":"Suggestive","shift_this_season":0.6957,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":0.1783,"enso_difference_p":0.3898,"trend_difference":-0.1579,"trend_difference_p":0.0435}},"values":[5.675,6.681,5.537,6.815,5.179,6.317,4.469,5.239,5.658,6.567,4.911,5.364,3.984,5.38,5.935,6.292,4.361,2.543,5.697,4.573,5.062,5.219,6.346,4.679,6.169,5.151,3.831,6.007,6.868,5.369,4.136,5.037,5.316,3.973,5.247,4.362,6.339,5.486,6.116,6.266,6.125,6.239,6.32,5.684,6.728,5.189,5.848,6.772,7.635,5.56